WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.817
These two tables can represent the same business facts even though they look different.

00:00:06.817 --> 00:00:12.147
In long form, Laptop January and Laptop February are two rows.

00:00:12.147 --> 00:00:18.816
In wide form, those two values appear on one Laptop row under separate month columns.

00:00:19.266 --> 00:00:22.828
This is why reshaping is not simply a visual change.

00:00:22.828 --> 00:00:28.848
The row meaning changes. Before you reshape, say the grain out loud.

00:00:28.848 --> 00:00:37.273
For example: one row per product and month before the reshape, and one row per product after the reshape.

00:00:37.273 --> 00:00:42.223
That simple habit makes the rest of the query much easier to reason about.
